<title>GERMANY: Buba's Palm-deficit slightly over 3 pct acceptable.</title>
<headline>Buba's Palm-deficit slightly over 3 pct acceptable.</headline>
<dateline>FREIBURG, Germany 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Guntram Palm said on Tuesday a 1997 budget deficit slightly over three percent reached without accounting tricks was preferable to a deficit of 2.9 percent aided by creative bookkeeping.</p>
<p>Palm said the main threat to the success of the European single currency did not lie in the extent of national budget deficits or public debt in 1997 but in the possibility that some participants may lack fiscal discipline after its launch.</p>
</text>
